WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.534
-Guys, it's Friday,
and that's usually when I write

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.868
my weekly thank-you notes.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.000
I was wondering if I could
do that right now.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.701
Do you guys mind?
-Yeah.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:07.767
-We do.
-Yes.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:10.567
-We don't.
-We do. We do.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.200
-No, we don't.
-We do!

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.033
-So, can I can some
thank-you note writing music,

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.267
please, Frannie?

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.267
[ Piano plays tender tune ]

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:19.901
Oh, perfect.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:23.067
First picture, please.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:26.267
Thank you, Oscar pools,
March Madness brackets,

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.534
and my taxes,
for being the three times a year

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:31.000
I fill out paperwork solely
through guessing.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.467
♪♪

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.234
One more time, Fran.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.400
♪♪
Thank you, Michelle Obama,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.000
for debuting
your new Netflix show,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.701
"Waffles &amp; Mochi," this week.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:43.734
And tune in next week

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.634
for Melania Trump's
new Netflix show,

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:47.367
"Waffles &amp; Mochi."

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:51.334
[ Laughing ]
♪♪

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.667
-You forgot about the picture.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.567
-Oh, yeah.
Show the next.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:55.767
Yeah, that was
"Waffles &amp; Mochi."

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.467
Thank you.
Good job, Winnie.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:58.601
♪♪

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.267
Thank you, Frannie.
Twice, even.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.934
♪♪

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.067
-Frannie --
-Thank you,

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:07.234
new study that three feet
of distance is enough

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.634
to keep students safe,
but to be extra safe,

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.100
all first graders
are still advised

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.000
to get a cootie shot.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.400
-What's a cootie shot?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.601
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:16.801
-[ Puffs ]

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.133
Thank you.
Go, Winnie.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.200
Go, Frannie.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.601
-I did this.

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:23.601
-Do one more, Winnie.

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:25.267
♪♪

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.701
Thank you, the president's
Help is Here" tour,

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.701
or, as most people
are calling it,

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.467
"Biden Better Have My Money."

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.467
[ Laughs ]
That's a song.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.968
Based off a song.

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:37.300
Frannie.
Having fun?

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.868
♪♪

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.868
Thank you -- Go, Win.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.300
-Go? Wait, what?
-Yeah, you can tap.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.934
Thank you, ribbons,

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.033
or, as I like to call you,

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.100
balloon leashes.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.901
♪♪

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.701
Lost Frannie.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:56.033
Thank you,
new Heinz condiments --

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.267
go, Winnie --

00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:00.934
Hanch, Wasabioli, and Tarchup,

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:02.467
for sounding like the name
of Iceland's

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:05.634
number-one personal injury firm.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.567
Oh, injury law firm.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.067
I was distracted by the silence.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.434
-[ Laughs ]
-You good?

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:14.934
Thank you, pogo sticks,

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.634
for being --
Frannie, still helping?

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:21.267
♪♪

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.701
[ Laughs ]

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:23.701
Tap, tap, tap, tap.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.734
That's a little dig.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.167
-Yep.
-That's very Frannie, yep.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.367
-Thank you, pogo sticks,
for being

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.267
jackhammers that
just want to have fun.

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:32.801
-[ Vocalizing ]
♪♪

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:33.868
[ Laughs ]
♪♪

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:36.100
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.100
Go, Winnie.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.734
Thank you, puzzles, for being

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.133
the slowest way possible

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:43.834
to download a picture.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.200
[ Thrumming music
joins piano tune ]

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.300
[ Laughs ]
-What are you doing?

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.000
[ Laughing ]

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.300
-Stop.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.133
-Just --

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:56.267
-Thank you,
hot chocolate fanatics --

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:58.534
[ Laughter ]
Go, Winnie.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:00.501
hot chocolate fanatics,
or, as I like to call you,

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:01.901
cocoa nuts.

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:03.434
♪♪

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.667
[ Chuckle ]

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:06.734
Final -- last one.

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:08.334
Winnie, last one.

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:09.400
[ Piano plays tender tune ]
There you go.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.667
-What?
-Yeah.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.167
-This one?
-Yeah, perfect.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.334
Thank you, salad,

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:15.267
for not being called
"wet leaves."

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.701
There you have it, everybody.

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:18.767
[ Laughing ]
Those are my thank-you notes.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:21.734
Thank you so much to my helpers.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.634
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.133
♪♪

